1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,645
Every morning, your coding agent wakes up brilliant.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:05,390
And remembers nothing.

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,209
It re-reads the same files,

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:11,591
misses the caller three hops away,

5
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,638
and re-applies the fix you reverted last spring.

6
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:18,400
Every session starts back at the trailhead.

7
00:00:18,450 --> 00:00:20,233
What if the trail remembered?

8
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,587
One command.

9
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:25,860
Meet Cairn. Institutional memory for coding agents.

10
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,078
A living map of your code.

11
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:33,255
The intent behind it, traced to every task.

12
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:36,447
What happened, and when it was true.

13
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,618
What your team learned, kept current.

14
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:45,000
And what every agent did, in one brief.

15
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:49,672
So tomorrow, your agent starts where today left off.

16
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:53,750
Three hundred sixty-nine times fewer tokens, for one answer.

17
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:56,214
Works with the agents you already use.

18
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:58,551
Cairn. Give your agents a memory.
